Yes. You can create an ArgoCD application using an application YAML file instead of the UI.

1. Create argocd-app.yaml
YAML
apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
kind: Application
metadata:
name: webapp
namespace: argocd
 
spec:
project: default
 
source:
repoURL: https://github.com/hyarel78/devmaster.git
targetRevision: master
path: myapp
 
destination:
server: https://kubernetes.default.svc
namespace: default
 
syncPolicy:
automated:
prune: true
selfHeal: true
 
syncOptions:
- CreateNamespace=true
2. Apply the Application
Shell
kubectl apply -f argocd-app.yaml
3. Verify
Shell
kubectl get applications -n argocd

Expected:

Plain Text
NAME SYNC STATUS HEALTH STATUS
webapp Synced Healthy
4. Check ArgoCD Application
Shell
kubectl describe application webapp -n argocd
5. Sync Manually (if Auto Sync is disabled)
Shell
argocd app sync webapp
6. See Deployed Resources
Shell
kubectl get deployment
kubectl get pods
kubectl get svc
Since your Helm chart is in GitHub:
Plain Text
devmaster/
└── myapp/
├── Chart.yaml
├── values.yaml
└── templates/

Use:

YAML
source:
repoURL: https://github.com/hyarel78/devmaster.git
targetRevision: master
path: myapp

ArgoCD will automatically detect Chart.yaml and treat myapp as a Helm chart.

Apply it:

Shell
kubectl apply -f argocd-app.yaml

and ArgoCD will deploy your Helm chart without creating the application through the UI.
